WHERE cricos_course_code = '120546A';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Organisations depend on effective project delivery to achieve strategic outcomes and employers increasingly value professionals who can lead projects while using data to improve decision‑making. Studying a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> with a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-project-management/">Master of Project Management</a> develops this capability by combining analytical insight with disciplined project leadership. You will build confidence in interpreting complex information, anticipating challenges, and supporting performance in fast‑paced organisational environments. <br/> <br/>Studying both master''s together equips you to manage projects across their full lifecycle while applying analytics to guide delivery. Graduates develop practical capability in coordinating scope, time, cost, quality, risk and stakeholders, alongside the ability to analyse project data and communicate insights clearly to diverse audiences. <br/><br/>Graduates stand out because they can link evidence with execution, manage complexity and deliver projects that achieve measurable, high‑quality results aligned with organisational goals. <br/> <br/>By completing this <a href="https://www.sydneybusinessschool.edu.au/study/two-masters-in-two-years/">double master’s program</a>, students will earn two master’s degrees in two years and build expertise in two in-demand areas of business. <br/> <br/>See the <a href="https://courses.uow.edu.au/courses/2026/3327?year=current">course handbook</a> for more information. </p><p>The <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/"></a><a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> equips you with advanced technical and analytical capability. You gain experience preparing and managing data, building dashboards, presenting insights, and applying analytics techniques such as forecasting, optimisation and machine learning. The program builds practical skills using tools such as Python, SQL, Power BI, SAS Viya and advanced Excel, ensuring you can deliver data‑driven recommendations in real business settings. </p><p>The <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/courses/master-of-project-management/"></a><a href="/study/courses/master-of-project-management/">Master of Project Managemen</a>t provides the knowledge and practical methods required to manage projects confidently from initiation through to closing. You explore project scoping, planning, execution, monitoring and completion, and learn strategies to manage scope, time, cost, quality, risk and stakeholder relationships. The program prepares you to respond effectively to the challenges encountered in contemporary project environments, ensuring you can coordinate teams, maintain project momentum, and deliver outcomes that align with organisational objectives.</p><p>You will learn to apply analytics within real project environments where delivery pressure, resource constraints and uncertainty are common. You gain experience using data to monitor progress, evaluate trade‑offs, and support timely decisions throughout a project’s lifecycle. The program also builds confidence working across technical and non‑technical teams, ensuring insights are communicated clearly and translated into practical actions.</p><p>By developing both analytical and project management capability, you will be prepared to support organisational change, improve delivery standards, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives. This integrated skill set enables you to play a key role in projects that require structured planning, clear communication, and evidence‑based leadership in complex, fast‑moving organisations. </p>',
    total_course_duration = '2 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91908,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><p>A range of admission options are available for future students. The procedures governing admission are defined in UOW''s <a href="https://documents.uow.edu.au/about/policy/ssLINK/UOW190887">Admissions Procedures</a>, and the UOW College <a href="https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/study/admissions-information/">Admissions Policy</a>.</p><p>For specific advice or to ask any questions regarding an application, please contact the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/contact/">UOW Future Students Team</a>.</p><ul><li><a href="#panel1">Entry Requirements </a></li><li><a href="#panel2">Additional information </a></li></ul><ul><li><a href="#">Academic Entry Requirements</a><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/><br/>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p></li><li><a href="#">English Language Requirements</a><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p> <table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p></li></ul><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/><br/>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p><p><strong>Reading</strong></p><p><strong>Writing</strong></p><p><strong>Listening</strong></p><p><strong>Speaking</strong></p><p>6.5</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>88</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p><ul><li><a href="#">Workload</a><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p> <p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p> <p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p></li><li><a href="#">Credit for Prior Learning</a><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p> <p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p> <p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p><p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p><p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p><p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p><p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.uow.edu.au/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics---master-of-project-management/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120534E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Modern supply chains rely on data to remain efficient, resilient and competitive. Employers are looking for graduates who can turn complex information into clear operational decisions. Studying a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> with a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-supply-chain-management/">Master of Supply Chain Management</a> prepares you to meet this need by developing strong analytical capability alongside an understanding of how supply chains function from end to end. You build the skills to analyse operational data, forecast demand, identify bottlenecks, and recommend improvements that strengthen supply performance. <br/> <br/>Studying these degrees together supports the analysis of complex business and supply chain environments, including demand patterns, operational constraints, data flows and organisational context, and applies this understanding to evidence based decision making. Students examine how organisations design, manage and optimise supply chains and how analytics can be used to translate data into actionable operational and strategic insights. <br/> <br/>Graduates stand out because they can link data to day‑to‑day supply chain decisions, support performance improvement and contribute to more efficient, productive and resilient operations across industries. <br/> <br/>By completing this <a href="https://www.sydneybusinessschool.edu.au/study/two-masters-in-two-years/">double master’s program</a>, students will earn two master’s degrees in two years and build expertise in two in-demand areas of business. <br/> <br/>See the <a href="https://courses.uow.edu.au/courses/2026/3328?year=current">course handbook</a> for more information. </p><p>The <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> equips you with advanced technical and analytical capability. You gain experience preparing and managing data, building dashboards, presenting insights and applying analytics techniques such as forecasting, optimisation and machine learning. The program builds practical skills using tools such as Python, SQL, Power BI, SAS Viya and advanced Excel, ensuring you can deliver data‑driven recommendations in real business settings. <br/> <br/>The <a href="/study/courses/master-of-supply-chain-management/">Master of Supply Chain Management</a> is designed for professionals who want to build or expand their capability in supply chain operations, procurement and logistics. The program develops the skills needed to manage the flow of goods, information and resources across modern organisations, preparing you to contribute to efficient, resilient and competitive supply chain performance. <br/> <br/>Graduates complete the program with the capability to work across disciplines and organisational levels. The combined study of business analytics and supply chain management strengthens the ability to collaborate with analysts, operations managers and senior leaders, ensuring that insights are communicated clearly and translated into action. This integrated approach prepares graduates to contribute to supply chain strategy, manage disruption, and support organisational responses to changing demand, risk and global operating conditions. </p>',
    total_course_duration = '2 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91908,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><p>A range of admission options are available for future students. The procedures governing admission are defined in UOW''s <a href="https://documents.uow.edu.au/about/policy/ssLINK/UOW190887">Admissions Procedures</a>, and the UOW College <a href="https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/study/admissions-information/">Admissions Policy</a>.</p><p>For specific advice or to ask any questions regarding an application, please contact the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/contact/">UOW Future Students Team</a>.</p><ul><li><a href="#panel1">Entry Requirements </a></li><li><a href="#panel2">Additional information </a></li></ul><ul><li><a href="#">Academic Entry Requirements</a><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR<br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/><br/>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p></li><li><a href="#">English Language Requirements</a><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p> <table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p></li></ul><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR<br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/><br/>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p><p><strong>Reading</strong></p><p><strong>Writing</strong></p><p><strong>Listening</strong></p><p><strong>Speaking</strong></p><p>6.5</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>88</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p><ul><li><a href="#">Workload</a><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p> <p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p> <p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p></li><li><a href="#">Credit for Prior Learning</a><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p> <p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p> <p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p><p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p><p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p><p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p><p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.uow.edu.au/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics---master-of-supply-chain-management/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120539M';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Modern organisations value employees who can analyse business performance and make evidence‑based decisions. Studying a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business/">Master of Business</a> with a <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> gives you the knowledge and skills to understand how organisations operate and how to use big data to analyse business performance.</p><p>Employers value graduates who can interpret data, uncover opportunities, and recommend actions that improve results. By studying both master''s, you will build strong business foundations while developing the ability to use analytics to improve outcomes and drive innovation.</p><p>You will gain comprehensive knowledge of core business disciplines, including management, strategy and organisational behaviour, and will develop the skills to apply this knowledge to real-world challenges.</p><p>By completing this <a href="https://www.sydneybusinessschool.edu.au/study/two-masters-in-two-years/">double master’s program</a>, students will earn two master’s degrees in two years and build expertise in two in-demand areas of business. </p><p>See the <a href="https://courses.uow.edu.au/courses/2026/3319?year=current">course handbook</a> for more information.</p><p>The <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business/">Master of Business</a> gives you the fundamental skills you need for a successful career in business, even if you come from a non‑business background. There is flexibility to choose the subjects that align with your professional development goals, allowing you to build your capability across key areas of organisational practice. </p><p>The <a href="/study/courses/master-of-business-analytics/">Master of Business Analytics</a> develops advanced skills in data analysis, artificial intelligence and machine learning, supporting evidence based decision making in contemporary organisations. </p><p>You will work across the full analytics lifecycle, from preparing and managing data to designing dashboards and visual narratives. You will use descriptive, predictive and prescriptive analytics techniques, including forecasting, optimisation and AI‑driven insights, to support clear and effective decision‑making. </p><p>You will work with industry tools such as Python, SQL, Power BI, SAS Viya and advanced Excel. Learn to generate insights, align them with organisational objectives and communicate them clearly to decision‑makers. </p><p>After finishing both master''s degrees, you will be uniquely positioned to bridge the gap between business and analytics. You will be prepared to lead data-informed initiatives, contribute to digital transformation, create measurable competitive advantage, and turn complex insights into meaningful action. </p>',
    total_course_duration = '2 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91908,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Entry Requirements</h4><p>A range of admission options are available for future students. The procedures governing admission are defined in UOW''s <a href="https://documents.uow.edu.au/about/policy/ssLINK/UOW190887">Admissions Procedures</a>, and the UOW College <a href="https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/study/admissions-information/">Admissions Policy</a>.</p><p>For specific advice or to ask any questions regarding an application, please contact the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/contact/">UOW Future Students Team</a>.</p><ul><li><a href="#panel1">Entry Requirements </a></li><li><a href="#panel2">Additional information </a></li></ul><ul><li><a href="#">Academic Entry Requirements</a><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. </p> <p>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p></li><li><a href="#">English Language Requirements</a><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p> <table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p></li></ul><p>A recognised bachelor’s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. <br/>OR <br/>A recognised master''s degree in any discipline with an equivalent average mark of 50%. </p><p>Other tertiary qualifications, combined with extensive professional work experience, may also be considered. </p><p>The following level of English is required to gain admission to this program:</p><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>English Test</strong></td> <td> <p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Reading</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Writing</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Listening</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>Speaking</strong></p> </td> </tr><tr><td>IELTS Academic</td> <td> <p>6.5</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> <td> <p>6.0</p> </td> </tr><tr><td>TOEFL (Internet-based)</td> <td> <p>88</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> <td> <p>18</p> </td> </tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Overall Score</strong></p><p><strong>Reading</strong></p><p><strong>Writing</strong></p><p><strong>Listening</strong></p><p><strong>Speaking</strong></p><p>6.5</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>6.0</p><p>88</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p>18</p><p><strong>UOW College:</strong> English for Tertiary Studies: Credit (weighted average mark of 65 overall and minimum 50 in Academic Reading and Writing) <br/><br/>Other qualifications may also be considered. Full details can be found on our <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/international/requirements/english/">English Language Requirements</a> website.</p><ul><li><a href="#">Workload</a><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p> <p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p> <p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p></li><li><a href="#">Credit for Prior Learning</a><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p> <p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p> <p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Full-Time Study Load</strong></p><p>As a full-time student, you can expect to commit around 48 hours of study per week. This includes class time and independent study. You may need to factor more time for examination study, practical work and placements.</p><p>For more details on course workloads, please refer to the <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/student/handbook/">UOW Handbook</a>.</p><p>If you have completed prior studies or relevant professional experience, you can request course credit or subject exemptions to reduce the duration and cost of your program.</p><p>Credit for prior learning evaluates your previous study or work experience related to your chosen subjects.</p><p>UOW values lifelong learning and recognises various types of prior learning, regardless of how or where it was obtained. For more information, refer to UOW''s <a href="https://www.uow.edu.au/study/credit-for-prior-learning/">Credit for Prior Learning page.</a></p>',
